# 20. The complete compiler-design picture

For your lab, remember this:

```text
             C-like Input
                   │
                   ▼
             ┌───────────┐
             │   FLEX    │
             │  Lexical  │
             │ Analysis  │
             └─────┬─────┘
                   │
                   │ Tokens
                   ▼
             ┌───────────┐
             │   YACC    │
             │  Syntax   │
             │ Analysis  │
             └─────┬─────┘
                   │
             ┌─────┴─────┐
             ▼           ▼
          Valid        Invalid
             │           │
             ▼           ▼
       Parse Success   yyerror()
```

### One-line explanation for viva:

> **FLEX identifies the individual tokens, while YACC uses grammar rules to determine whether those tokens form a syntactically valid switch statement.**

